<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Feb CPI seen rising 2.4 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Feb CPI seen rising 2.4 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists forecast Dutch February consumer price inflation would rise slightly to a year-on-year rate of 2.4 percent from 2.3 in January.</p>
<p>The February consumer inflation data is due to be published at 0930 GMT on Friday. Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p> GMT--Date-Period-Indicator------------Consensus--Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0930 07/3 Feb    CPI Mth/Mth	     0.4 pct    0.2/0.6   0.3</p>
<p> 0930 07/3 Feb    CPI Yr/Yr		 2.4 pct    2.1/2.6   2.3</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, MeesPierson, J.P. Morgan, NIBStrating, Rabobank. -- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
